# Line endings are decided here rather than by each contributor's
# `core.autocrlf`. This harness is developed on Windows and read on Linux, and
# without this a contributor whose git does not normalise commits a whole file of
# changed line endings around a one-line change, which buries the change in the
# diff.
#
# It does not affect the committed query lists, which are verified byte for byte
# against their generator: `build_queries.py --check` compares through
# `read_text`, and text mode normalises newlines on the way in, so the check
# passes whichever ending is on disk. Stated because it is the one place where a
# newline could have been load-bearing.
* text=auto

# Committed inputs and evidence, in the endings they are generated with.
*.txt text
*.jsonl text
*.toml text
*.md text
*.py text
*.yml text
